{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1292","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Nora's Toy Boxes"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://soundcloud.com/hanatsuka/sihanatsuka-ember"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"SIHanatsuka - EMber"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://soundcloud.com/hanatsuka/sihanatsuka-atonement"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"SIHanatsuka - ATONEMENT"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Back in time, the seven-year-old Nora used to play lots of games with her creation ROBO_Head-02, both to have fun and enhance his abilities."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One day, Nora's adoptive father, Phoenix Wyle, brought Nora $$$n$$$ boxes of toys. Before unpacking, Nora decided to make a fun game for ROBO."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"She labelled all $$$n$$$ boxes with $$$n$$$ distinct integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ and asked ROBO to do the following action several (possibly zero) times:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Pick three distinct indices $$$i$$$, $$$j$$$ and $$$k$$$, such that $$$a_i \\mid a_j$$$ and $$$a_i \\mid a_k$$$. In other words, $$$a_i$$$ divides both $$$a_j$$$ and $$$a_k$$$, that is $$$a_j \\bmod a_i = 0$$$, $$$a_k \\bmod a_i = 0$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After choosing, Nora will give the $$$k$$$-th box to ROBO, and he will place it on top of the box pile at his side. Initially, the pile is empty. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After doing so, the box $$$k$$$ becomes unavailable for any further actions. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Being amused after nine different tries of the game, Nora asked ROBO to calculate the number of possible different piles having the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"largest"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" amount of boxes in them. Two piles are considered different if there exists a position where those two piles have different boxes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Since ROBO was still in his infant stages, and Nora was still too young to concentrate for a long time, both fell asleep before finding the final answer. Can you help them?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As the number of such piles can be very large, you should print the answer modulo $$$10^9 + 7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 60$$$), denoting the number of boxes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ distinct integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 60$$$), where $$$a_i$$$ is the label of the $$$i$$$-th box."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the number of distinct piles having the maximum number of boxes that ROBO_Head can have, modulo $$$10^9 + 7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n2 6 8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2 3 4 9 12\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n5 7 2 9\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's illustrate the box pile as a sequence $$$b$$$, with the pile's bottommost box being at the leftmost position."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, there are $$$2$$$ distinct piles possible: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$b = [6]$$$ ($$$[2, \\mathbf{6}, 8] \\xrightarrow{(1, 3, 2)} [2, 8]$$$) "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$b = [8]$$$ ($$$[2, 6, \\mathbf{8}] \\xrightarrow{(1, 2, 3)} [2, 6]$$$) "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, there are $$$4$$$ distinct piles possible: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$b = [9, 12]$$$ ($$$[2, 3, 4, \\mathbf{9}, 12] \\xrightarrow{(2, 5, 4)} [2, 3, 4, \\mathbf{12}] \\xrightarrow{(1, 3, 4)} [2, 3, 4]$$$) "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$b = [4, 12]$$$ ($$$[2, 3, \\mathbf{4}, 9, 12] \\xrightarrow{(1, 5, 3)} [2, 3, 9, \\mathbf{12}] \\xrightarrow{(2, 3, 4)} [2, 3, 9]$$$) "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$b = [4, 9]$$$ ($$$[2, 3, \\mathbf{4}, 9, 12] \\xrightarrow{(1, 5, 3)} [2, 3, \\mathbf{9}, 12] \\xrightarrow{(2, 4, 3)} [2, 3, 12]$$$) "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$b = [9, 4]$$$ ($$$[2, 3, 4, \\mathbf{9}, 12] \\xrightarrow{(2, 5, 4)} [2, 3, \\mathbf{4}, 12] \\xrightarrow{(1, 4, 3)} [2, 3, 12]$$$) "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third sequence, ROBO can do nothing at all. Therefore, there is only $$$1$$$ valid pile, and that pile is empty."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1292F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1292/problem/F"}